{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights","id":1367935,"title":"Combat Movement - how mobile are your fights?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-14T17:48:04-08:00","id":1367935,"title":"Combat Movement - how mobile are your fights?","content":"I tend to picture Exalted combat as a fairly mobile affair. No-one's standing still while the action is happening - characters in hand to hand are running through the street kicking carts at each other between swings, archers are hopping from building to building while taking shots, switching targets to help an ally is fairly common.<br /> <br /> However, we ran into an odd issue in our latest session, revolving around the Disengage action. <br /> <br /> If you want to move towards a different enemy while in melee, you need a good Dodge+Dexterity roll to do so.<br /> <br /> Without charms that let you close the distance to different enemies out of range, any non-Trivial enemy will tarpit a character in melee until incapacitated or knocked prone. On top of that, you need to use a specific skill to move around in the fight. If an ally is at short distance and needs your help but you've got a bad Dodge+Dexterity pool they might as well be on another planet. Hell, 4 Solars could be outnumbering a Dragon 4 to 1, but until that Dragon dies they can't help their friend who's fighting the other 4 shikari without passing a challenge. <br /> <br /> As our game currently has 2 people going down the Strength and Stamina Lunar subsitution route for combat, we're left in the weird position where there is literally no ability for half the Circle to move once battle is joined. We can Rush but can't do anything about it, as there's no Strength or Stamina charms that let you shrug off attacks while rushing to an ally's aid. Functionally, combat is much less mobile than we'd thought. <br /> <br /> Has this been an issue in anyone else's game, or is there something I'd missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6706-meetcute","name":"MeetCute","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:07:23-08:00","id":1367940,"title":"","content":"Well, also keep in mind that a character will only prevent another character from moving if they <i>choose</i> to do so. I don\u2019t imagine your guy getting dogpiled by four Solars is really going to object to one of them electing to walk away and <i>not</i> keep beating his teeth out.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if a person\u2019s got no means by which to oppose a mover\u2019s movement, they can\u2019t oppose the movement; a ground-based brawler with no reach weapon is probably going to be penalized at minimum when trying to stop a sparrow flying two yards over his head, and a swordsman who lacks Charms to interact with dematerialized spirits will not be able to stop an intangible ghost from walking into a room.<br /> <br /> Sure, if a character elects to completely dump Dexterity and Dodge, they\u2019re often going to have difficulty escaping a determined attacker. But not always - a creative PC might use his cunning to conceal a bear trap where the fight takes place, wait for the enemy to step into it, and then leisurely walk away. Or use his Joint-Wounding Attack to specifically injure his enemy\u2019s legs before trying to make his escape. I don\u2019t see this as a bug; if you have a disadvantage and do nothing to either mitigate it or level the playing field, it\u2019s going to hold you back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-14-2020, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T19:33:33-08:00","id":1367955,"title":"","content":"About <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U9n5Tbj9m3s\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> mobile.<br /> <br /> As for disengages to move between opponents in a battle, I only call for disengage actions when a character cares about getting away from their opponent (so, if you're just trying to move towards a doorway but don't actually care about getting away from the other guy, there would be no need to disengage), or when an opponent is specifically trying to prevent a character from moving in some particular way (towards an ally, towards a recently disarmed daiklaive, etc). Otherwise I don't call for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:23:37-08:00","id":1367986,"title":"","content":"I've encountered issues with the tar pit before now. Though my experience is mostly Melee Solars who treat Dodge as completely superfluous because that's what they did in 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T00:42:04-08:00","id":1368005,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that happened to my Melee 5 assassin, he got stuck fighting a mortal guard while the target put on his armour, because I had Dodge 2 and no excellency.<br /> <br /> My fights are generally very mobile stunt-wise, with people leaping, swinging, etc. And charging into combat. But once there, they'll stay for a bit. I haven't had big issues with it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T13:59:21-08:00","id":1368122,"title":"","content":"System working as intended. You can't just put a Five in one Ability and be good at combat. You need all the Abilities marked (in bold) <b>This Ability is important in combat</b>.<br /> <br /> And remember, it's only the normal Reflexive move action that can't be used. If you have a Charm that moves you, then you move.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, Dodge is important in combat.<br /> <br /> If you make a big, strong brute who isn't very mobile, then they're not going to be very mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-15-2020, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T14:05:08-08:00","id":1368124,"title":"","content":"Considering that for a swordsman, Dodge is otherwise only there for the occasional unblockable attack (whereas in real life a master swordsman would also be good at dodging attacks, you can't parry everything), I agree that it's probably a good thing that you need it for Disengage.<br /> <br /> Still, even if you do have it, Disengage needs 2i and a roll, so there's probably not going to be a ton of Disengaging even when people are good at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:50:19-08:00","id":1368156,"title":"","content":"In the Narrative, Monkey Leap and runs, jumps, flips, side rolls, etc are all happening every round. Mechanically, my players seldom try to get to specific places and just kill the enemy closest to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T16:22:10-08:00","id":1368165,"title":"","content":"The real advantage of Monkey Leap technique in combat is if you're fighting a master Air Dragon stylist in an area that's covered in difficult terrain you can chase after him without spending two whole turns just to even attempt a rush each time. Note that difficult terrain can also be climbing up ladders to reach a wall above you or any other such thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T17:12:39-08:00","id":1368173,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember is that you can be very mobile in fluff terms without your movement doing much re: range bands.<br /> <br /> As far as actual disengages and such, I've seen some but not constant disengaging. I personally always have my characters with at least solid Dodge capacity (I have some slightly weird personal minima my characters nearly always, so I never really have had to deal with the &quot;whoops my disengage is real bad&quot; problem myself. However, I often don't invest much in Athletics; thus my characters are good at disengaging, but not so good at opposing disengages or being on either side of a rush.<br /> <br /> Also, re: the problem of 4 Solars being tarpitted by a single DB, besides the fact that the DB might be content to get a Solar off their back, there's also the fact that a character being so dogpiled is at not insignificant risk of being rendered less capable of opposing a hopeful escapee. Beyond simply being incapacitated or even just wounded enough to penalize their anti-disengage rolls significantly, a character who is prone or who is being grappled cannot normally oppose disengage attempts. I like this, since it offers more ways to assist oneself or one's allies when disengaging gets difficult.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also remembered, regarding DBs, that they have two rather neat Charms that each allow a character to enhance a combat movement with Performance or Sail, respectively. While it costs motes and initiative, it's still a way for someone who might have poor standard movement investment (in my case, it'll be poor Athletics more than poor Dodge) to whip out a good movement pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 02-16-2020, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T17:59:12-08:00","id":1368188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights?p=1368165#post1368165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real advantage of Monkey Leap technique in combat is if you're fighting a master Air Dragon stylist in an area that's covered in difficult terrain you can chase after him without spending two whole turns just to even attempt a rush each time. Note that difficult terrain can also be climbing up ladders to reach a wall above you or any other such thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I have Stormwind RIder on my Melee Dawn. How do ya like me now, flyers and archers? How do you like it!? (He has an Intimacy of hating archers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T00:07:16-08:00","id":1368233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights?p=1368124#post1368124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that for a swordsman, Dodge is otherwise only there for the occasional unblockable attack (whereas in real life a master swordsman would also be good at dodging attacks, you can't parry everything), I agree that it's probably a good thing that you need it for Disengage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You'll probably survive being unable to disengage effectively and learn for next time, inability to parry tends to not be a mistake you'll live long enough to repeat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T04:41:17-08:00","id":1368891,"title":"","content":"Must say for the moment I've been pretty unsatisfied with the movement. I've rarely seen someone use a disengage for another reason that &quot;I'm not a fighter and I want to flee before I die&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:05:07-08:00","id":1368901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights?p=1368891#post1368891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've rarely seen someone use a disengage for another reason that &quot;I'm not a fighter and I want to flee before I die&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my seafaring game, one of the PCs got forced underwater by a demon during a fight, and one of the others disengaged with the demon he was fighting to pull her out.<br /> <br /> (Also, I\u2019d argue that an Archery Supernal Dawn is just as much of a fighter as a Melee Supernal Dawn, even if he\u2019s not enthusiastic about having a Melee Supernal Dawn in his face.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:13:42-08:00","id":1368903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights?p=1368901#post1368901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my seafaring game, one of the PCs got forced underwater by a demon during a fight, and one of the others disengaged with the demon he was fighting to pull her out.<br /> <br /> (Also, I\u2019d argue that an Archery Supernal Dawn is just as much of a fighter as a Melee Supernal Dawn, even if he\u2019s not enthusiastic about having a Melee Supernal Dawn in his face.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the kind of situations I'd like to see more but they were very rare in my games. <br /> <br /> I won't really argue about Archers and stuff I sadly never got any in my games","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:23:12-08:00","id":1368904,"title":"","content":"I think certainly having a party full of close-combat fighters is going to lead to far less Disengage than a group full of horse archers or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:26:53-08:00","id":1368906,"title":"","content":"I guess this makes sense. I tried having multiple kind of enemies that were mobile but the players never really bothered by trying to target a specific moving enemy, they usually went straight in and blowed the first thing they found.<br /> <br /> I might try to suggest doing more varied combat ability characters in my next campaign","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:34:05-08:00","id":1368908,"title":"","content":"I had a great combat last week with a demon trying to Restrain/Drag to split the party whilst their allies tarpitted. Very tense dramatic moment as Cynis Ganan rolls 5 dice to Disengage (being another big slow brute).<br /> <br /> I kinda feel like Disengage should <i>grant</i> two Initiative instead of causing you to lose two. Initiative is supposed to represent you &quot;seiz[ing] the upper hand during the course of battle&quot; so you can &quot;the proper moment to capitalize on [your] advantage with a decisive blow&quot;. How does putting yourself in a better position hurt that? Surely putting yourself in a better position <i>helps</i> you?<br /> <br /> IDK, I haven't playtested it but strongly considering it for a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:35:29-08:00","id":1368910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights?p=1368906#post1368906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess this makes sense. I tried having multiple kind of enemies that were mobile but the players never really bothered by trying to target a specific moving enemy, they usually went straight in and blowed the first thing they found.<br /> <br /> I might try to suggest doing more varied combat ability characters in my next campaign</div> </div> </div> </div>Try a Celestial level sorcerer with Blood Apes. That'd strongly incentivise the PCs to ignore the melee fighters and go for the ranged character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:39:19-08:00","id":1368912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367935-combat-movement-how-mobile-are-your-fights?p=1368910#post1368910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try a Celestial level sorcerer with Blood Apes. That'd strongly incentivise the PCs to ignore the melee fighters and go for the ranged character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's a good idea, I actually had a very mobile PC last game that could fly with Stormwind rider and was very effective because not all ennemies had range attacks, and he also had the Virtuous Guardian of Flame which made him very hard to hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T11:51:05-08:00","id":1368983,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Melee-ists getting stuck in combat, you may want to suggest they take Nimble Reaving Wind, from Miracles of the Solar Exalted. 1m, lets you move from one opponent to another in short range and attack, without needing to make a Disengage roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}